## Fold describe_entity BFS traversal into one server-side query (263s → ~34s)

Context: MCP QA testing hit 502s on "heavy depth-2 scans". Measurement showed
the 502 is a latency symptom, not a warehouse-capacity problem: a Medium/4-cluster
warehouse gave 0% improvement over Small/1-cluster, and the warehouse sat
near-idle. The `describe_entity` data path (`/api/v1/digitaltwin/triples/find`
→ `DigitalTwin.find_triples_bfs`) was the bottleneck. For a type-wide scan
(`entity_type="Counterparty", depth=2`): the recursive BFS discovered ~20,920
entities (59.5s, on the 60s statement-timeout edge), then `get_triples_for_subjects`
fetched ~366,284 triples with no DISTINCT/LIMIT, which were de-duplicated in
Python and sliced to 100. Two isolated fixes were verified against the live
warehouse before implementation: (a) folding traversal+fetch+dedup+pagination
into one query removes the ~200s of Python materialisation; (b) replacing the
non-sargable OR-join with a bidirectional-edge UNION cuts the CTE ~60s→~32s.
Combined, the folded query returns the same first 100-triple page in ~34.5s
(7.6×), with no change to the triples returned.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py
   Added `_bfs_edge_filter` (shared edge predicate) and `_bfs_walk_cte`
   (bidirectional-edge recursive walk) helpers. Rewrote `bfs_traversal` to use
   the sargable single-equality edge join instead of the OR-join. Added
   `find_triples_bfs_page` (folds seed → BFS → triple fetch → DISTINCT → ORDER
   BY → LIMIT/OFFSET into one query; fetches limit+1 to derive `has_more`
   without a COUNT) and `count_seeds`.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   Rewrote `find_triples_bfs` to delegate to `store.count_seeds` +
   `store.find_triples_bfs_page`; removed the in-Python dedup loop and
   post-fetch slice. Return payload now carries `has_more` instead of the
   expensive `total`/`entity_count`. Alias expansion is no longer applied on
   this path (it re-materialised the full entity set); `expand_uri_aliases`
   remains for its other callers.
3. src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py
   `FindResponse`: replaced `total`/`entity_count` with `has_more`. Route maps
   the new field and logs page count + has_more.
4. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Session-aware `/dtwin/triples/find` payload aligned to `has_more`.
5. src/mcp-server/server/tools.py
   `describe_entity`: added performance guidance to the docstring (entity-scoped
   deep scans via `search`; keep `depth=1` for type-wide scans). Updated the
   stale `total` comment to `has_more`.
6. src/mcp-server/server/formatting.py, src/agents/tools/graph_formatting.py
   `_format_find_response` uses `has_more` (shows "N+ triples" and a
   "more exist" hint) instead of `total`.
7. src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jReadOps.py, Neo4jStore.py
   Added `count_seeds` and `find_triples_bfs_page` Cypher overrides so the
   non-SQL backend keeps the abstract contract (walk from structured
   search/entity_type seeds, de-dup and paginate in Python).
8. tests/units/dtwin/test_digitaltwin_api.py
   Wired the SQL-capture harness to the real `_bfs_walk_cte`/`_sql_relation`
   helpers; added tests for the bidirectional-edge join, folded-page
   DISTINCT/ORDER/LIMIT+1 and `has_more`, and `count_seeds`.
9. tests/back/core/digitaltwin/test_digitaltwin_units.py
   Added `TestFindTriplesBfs` covering delegation, `has_more`, and the
   no-seeds short-circuit (no page query issued).

